{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Why should we be diminished.</b> He said to them: consecrated offerings are not brought in impurity. They said to him: let the blood be sprinkled upon us by pure priests, and let the flesh be eaten by those who are pure. He said to them: ״Stand, and I will hear״ — like a disciple confident of hearing from his teacher's mouth. Happy is he who was born of a woman who is thus confident, that whenever he wished he would speak with the Shekhinah; and this passage was fit to be said through Moses like the rest of the entire Torah, except that these merited that it be said through them — for merit is drawn through the meritorious (there)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:04.387911804Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}